END OF MATERIAL

Write up to {{ count }} questions drawn from the passages above.

For each question set:
  topic     two to five words naming what is being tested
  question  self-contained; a student should be able to answer it without
            seeing the passage it came from
  answer    complete, and supported by the material
  source    the file name shown in brackets above, exactly as written
  page      the page number shown in brackets above

Spread the questions across different passages. Do not write two questions
that test the same point. If a passage is administrative, a citation, or a
fragment of a table, skip it.
